    The n stones occupy the first n cells, with two empty cells at the
    end. A move transfers any adjacent occupied pair into the empty pair,
    preserving its order. Both empty cells must again be at the end in
    the target configuration. Return -1 if the target is unreachable.

    Args:
        n: Number of stones (2 <= n <= 14).
        s: Initial string of B and W stones, of length n.
        t: Target string of B and W stones, of length n.
